---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'October 9, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for CodesCompiler, including information about cookies, Google AdSense, analytics, and user choices."
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 bg-white shadow-sm my-8 rounded-lg">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-8"><strong>Last Updated:</strong> {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose prose-brand prose-lg max-w-none">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how CodesCompiler ("CodesCompiler", "we", "us", or "our")
        handles information when you visit and use <strong>codescompiler.com</strong> and
        <strong>app.codescompiler.com</strong>, including our tutorials, articles, programming
        examples, interactive tools, and other educational resources.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>
        CodesCompiler is primarily an educational website. You can read most of our content
        without creating an account or directly providing personal information.
      </p>
      <p>
        Depending on how you use the website, information may be processed automatically,
        such as your IP address, browser type, device information, approximate location,
        pages viewed, referring pages, and technical information needed to operate and secure
        the website.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you contact us, we may receive the name, email address, and other information that
        you choose to include in your message.
      </p>

      <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To operate, maintain, and improve CodesCompiler.</li>
        <li>To provide tutorials, examples, tools, and interactive coding features.</li>
        <li>To understand website usage and improve content and performance.</li>
        <li>To respond to questions, feedback, and support requests.</li>
        <li>To protect the website against abuse, fraud, spam, and security threats.</li>
        <li>To display and measure advertising where advertising is enabled.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Google AdSense and Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        We may use Google AdSense and other advertising partners to help support the free
        availability of our educational content. Third-party advertising providers may use
        cookies or similar technologies to show, personalize, measure, and limit advertising.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google may use information about your visits to this and other websites to provide
        advertising services. The use of advertising cookies is subject to Google's applicable
        policies and your available privacy choices.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can review or manage Google's advertising personalization choices through
        <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google My Ad Center</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Google Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We may use Google Analytics to understand how visitors use CodesCompiler, such as
        which pages are visited and how visitors navigate the website. Analytics information
        helps us improve the site's content, usability, and performance.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies and similar technologies may be used for essential website functionality,
        preferences, analytics, security, and advertising. Some cookies may be placed by
        third-party services used on the website.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can control or delete cookies through your browser settings. Blocking certain
        cookies may affect some website features or advertising functionality.
      </p>
      <p>
        For more information about cookies used on CodesCompiler, please see our
        <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Third-Party Websites and Services</h2>
      <p>
        CodesCompiler may link to third-party websites, services, documentation, social
        networks, advertisements, or other resources. Those services operate under their
        own privacy policies and terms. We encourage you to review their policies before
        providing personal information.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        CodesCompiler provides educational material that may be useful to students and
        younger learners. We do not knowingly request personal information from children
        for the purpose of creating accounts or profiles. If you believe a child has
        provided personal information to us, please contact us so we can review the request.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Data Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect information
        handled through the website. However, no internet transmission or storage system
        can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Your Choices</h2>
      <p>
        You may control cookies through your browser, manage Google's advertising choices
        through Google My Ad Center, and contact us if you have questions about information
        submitted directly to CodesCompiler.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy when our website, services, advertising,
        analytics, or legal requirements change. The updated version will be published on
        this page with a revised "Last Updated" date.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or privacy at CodesCompiler, please
        contact us at
        <a href="mailto:contact@codescompiler.com">contact@codescompiler.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
